GNU Go 3.8 will not cross-compile for Windows with a current mingw-w64: two
declarations of verifyW32() in utils/gg_utils.c use an implicit int return type,
which C99 removed and modern GCC rejects outright.

This is the *only* change made to the upstream sources. It is recorded here
because the Windows bundles distributed from hraj.si contain GNU Go binaries
built from these sources, and GPLv3 obliges us to offer the corresponding
source — which means upstream's tarball *plus this patch*, not upstream's
tarball alone.

Upstream:  https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gnugo/gnugo-3.8.tar.gz
sha256:    da68d7a65f44dcf6ce6e4e630b6f6dd9897249d34425920bfdd4e07ff1866a72

Verified 2026-08-28 by diffing the whole build tree against that tarball:
2256 files identical, this one differing, no files added or removed. The extra
.c files under patterns/ are generated by GNU Go's own mkpat at build time.

--- a/utils/gg_utils.c	2009-02-17 22:41:31.000000000 +0100
+++ b/utils/gg_utils.c	2026-01-19 14:20:52.016070534 +0100
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@
 #ifdef VC
 #include <crtdbg.h>
 
-verifyW32(BOOL b)
+static void verifyW32(BOOL b)
 {
   if (!b) {
     _ASSERTE(0 && "Win32 Error");
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@
 
 #else
 /* mingw32 lacks crtdbg.h and _ASSERTE */
-verifyW32(BOOL b)
+static void verifyW32(BOOL b)
 {
   if (!b) {
     fprintf(stderr, "Win32 Err: %ld\n", GetLastError());
